# turnstile - checks that must pass before a push leaves this repo.
#
#   <name>: <shell command>
#
# Run from the repo root. Non-zero exit refuses the push.
# Delete this file and the repo passes straight through.
#
# Keep these fast. A gate that takes two minutes is a gate you will start
# bypassing, and a bypassed gate is worse than no gate - it costs time AND
# trains you to ignore it.

lint: make lint
test: go test ./...

# Available to each command, so checks can scope themselves to the push
# instead of walking the whole repo:
#
#   TURNSTILE_RANGE          e.g. abc123..def456
#   TURNSTILE_CHANGED_FILES  newline-separated paths in that range
#
# changed-tests: go test $(echo "$TURNSTILE_CHANGED_FILES" | xargs -n1 dirname | sort -u)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ai modules
#
#   ai <name>: block=<level> [model=<model>]
#
# Model-backed checks. These run in parallel with each other and with the
# commands above, so they add wall-clock once rather than once per module.
#
# `block` is the lowest severity that refuses the push - low, medium, high,
# critical, or `never` to report without ever blocking. Findings below the line
# still print, marked `advisory`.
#
# Results are cached on a hash of the diff + the module's source, so re-pushing
# the same commits is free. A module that cannot run prints `?` and lets the
# push through rather than blocking on a network blip.

ai review:  block=high
ai secrets: block=medium

# Two built-ins ship: `review` (correctness defects provable from the diff) and
# `secrets` (credentials about to be published). Override either, or add your
# own, by dropping a markdown file with frontmatter in:
#
#   .turnstile.d/modules/<name>.md    this repo only
#   ~/.turnstile/modules/<name>.md    all your repos
#
# `turnstile status` prints which file each name actually resolved to.
